    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight mb-4 text-white">
      Pergola Rafter Span &amp; Cantilever Rules: Sizing Tables
    </h1>

    <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-300 max-w-3xl mb-6 leading-relaxed">
      Unlike residential roofs, an unroofed pergola does not carry heavy shingles or plywood decking. However, it must resist self-weight sagging over long clear spans, wet snow accumulation on top purlins, and fierce wind uplift forces that can tear rafters off beams.
    </p>

    <!-- Key Metrics Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-700/60 text-left">
      <div>
        <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-400 font-semibold">Max 2x8 Span (16" OC)</div>
        <div class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-sky-400">13 Ft - 6 In</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-400 font-semibold">Max 2x10 Span (16" OC)</div>
        <div class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-emerald-400">17 Ft - 2 In</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-400 font-semibold">Max Cantilever Rule</div>
        <div class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-amber-400">L / 4 Maximum</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-400 font-semibold">Recommended Post Size</div>
